WEBVTT

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.200
"Teachers' Room"

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.080
"Teachers' Room"
Mr. Takinami. Um...
About the title of that piece...

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.790
"Tenkyu"
"A bow in the heavens"... "Tenkyu," huh?

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:28.500
Yes. I originally thought of "Rainbow,"
but I thought it might be too obvious.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.620
Why "Rainbow"?

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.200
I-I thought that the rainbow
that comes after the rain

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.450
is kind of like our smiles...
since there are seven of us...

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:37.950
"Hahaha!
Seven club members"

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:38.950
"Hahaha!
Seven club members"
"Rainbow (a bow in the heavens)
Seven colors...?"

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.540
A rainbow with seven colors, huh?

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.250
That's good.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.910
On second thought, I'll change it!

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:49.910
Wait, wait. I really think it's good.
But I want to change just one character.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:51.450
From "bow" to "cry."
This is still read "Tenkyu," so...

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:56.410
"Ten (sky) kyu (bow)
kyu (cry)"
From "bow" to "cry."
This is still read "Tenkyu," so...

00:00:56.410 --> 00:01:01.870
"The heavens cry"? So this piece
really does give off a sad impression?

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:04.160
I didn't say that.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.120
Tenkyu with "cry" is the rain that falls
even when there's no cloud.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:14.540
This is just my impression, but I think it's like
the rain that falls from a clear blue sky.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.450
People cry for different reasons, right?
Not just when they're sad.

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:24.700
It seems like you understand
this piece a lot better than I do.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.450
If I didn't, that'd be a problem.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:30.660
Unless I understand it better,
I can't give you guidance, can I?

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.450
The title has been decided.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:40.330
But what they still seriously lack is...

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:44.200
Mr. Takinami. Do you have a minute?

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.580
"#18 Their Determination"

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.200
"#18 Their Determination"
Oh? Are you gonna be
sitting behind me, Kurusu?

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.660
What?! You're sitting in front of me?!

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:25.750
I feel kinda bad that even our seats are close.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.620
It's like we're constantly together
if you count our club time.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:31.040
"Seating Rearrangement"
No, not at all! Rather, I'm happy!

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.370
What?

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.290
Y-You know, it's easier to
discuss club activities this way!

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.450
I'm happy in that sense!

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.540
Oh, yeah, you're right.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.410
Th-That was close. Good thing he's dense.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.870
Wow...

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:54.250
Thank you, God! I'll work hard
on club stuff! I'll work super hard!

00:03:55.250 --> 00:04:00.790
My name is Dojima. I'm from
Ikuta Style Koto Hozuki School.

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:07.660
We heard that the daughter of our grand master
is a member of your koto club.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:13.700
So if there's anything we can do,
we definitely would like to be of help.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:14.540
"Koto Club"

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.080
"Koto Club"
"Tenkyu"?!

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:21.790
Wow... It sounds kinda pretty.
The rain that falls even when it's sunny?

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:22.660
Oh, Mr. Takinami.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.370
What, not everyone's here yet?

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:29.370
Ah... Kudo and the others
are on cleaning duty, so--

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:34.580
Hello, Satowa.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:40.330
M-Miss Dojima... Why...?

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.080
You know her, Hozuki?

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:48.830
I am Akira Dojima from the Hozuki School.
Nice to meet you.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:53.870
Starting today, I'll be giving you koto lessons.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.080
I appreciate this opportunity.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.080
What?! K-Koto lessons?

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:01.370
And she's from the Hozuki School?!

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.870
Hey, Suzu! What's the meaning of this?!

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.330
This? It's exactly how it sounds.

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.410
That's not what I meant!

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.910
Whooooa! Chika! I'm gonna beat you today!

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.120
In your dreams!

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:17.870
Whoosh!

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.950
You idiots...!

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:26.290
So cool, we fell over like dominos!

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:34.160
Mr. Takinami. What're these students doing?

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:37.450
Oh, I'm sorry for the commotion.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:40.540
They're koto club members, too.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.370
You're kidding, right?

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:44.080
No.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.410
Mr. Takinami, who's this lady?

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.790
Starting today, she's your koto teacher.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:50.450
Huh?!

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.790
On top of that, she's from the Hozuki School.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:57.830
I thought you were going to
give us guidance, Mr. Takinami.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:01.950
I will... I'll give you musical guidance
on the piece as a whole.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:06.830
But what you need the most right now
is to improve your technique.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:11.160
No matter how outstanding one's musicality is
or how deeply it can touch people,

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:14.370
if their technique is inferior,
they can't win in a competition.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:19.120
And unfortunately,
I can't teach you koto.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:23.250
But we've got Hozuki. If she teaches us
like she has been, then--

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:27.200
I want her to focus on her own practice.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:32.500
It's quite a burden to teach others
while you're playing.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:35.580
You lose quite a bit of
practice time for yourself, too.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:41.080
Or did you guys think that Hozuki doesn't
need to practice or something?

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:45.080
So, if you get it,
then start practicing already.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:50.540
I'd like to know your abilities,
so I'll just watch today.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:54.750
It's true that it's better to have a koto teacher.

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:57.200
But why does it have to be Miss Dojima?

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.290
What do I do if she's trying
to pull something on the club?

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.700
If something happens to
the others because of me...

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.450
Hozuki.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.950
You don't have to worry about anything.

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:10.620
It'll be fine, so practice
as much as you'd like.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.500
Mr. Takinami...

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.250
Now, you guys, too.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:24.200
This is the sheet music for the piece
they're practicing right now.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:25.950
Thank you very much.

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.040
I've never heard of this piece before.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.000
It's an original piece, so...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.120
I see... Then first I need to learn
about this piece, too.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.870
"Koto Club"

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:03.200
So what do you think after
watching their practice?

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:09.870
Well... I'm disappointed that their
skill level is lower than what I expected.

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:13.200
It seems that Satowa has been
teaching them until now,

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.040
but her teaching must have been quite sloppy.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:16.870
Huh?!

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:20.620
You sound pretty arrogant,
but are you really that good?

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:22.410
What do you mean by "that good"?

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.870
Can you play better than Hozuki?

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:29.000
I think teaching and playing
require totally different talents.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.370
But well...

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:34.290
Satowa played the original piece,
"Tenkyu," and was disqualified

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:37.200
in the National Koto Competition.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.080
And I'm the one who won first place
in that same competition.

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:49.160
Is that satisfactory to you?

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:49.750
"Nishina Instruments"

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.660
Arrrgh! Who does she think she is?!

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:54.500
"Is that satisfactory to you?"

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.450
She ticks me off!

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.750
I don't like her, either!

00:08:56.750 --> 00:09:01.000
I bet she's planning to mess up our club,
just like I was before!

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.870
Kurusu. Calm down.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:04.700
--If I remember correctly,
--Huh?! How can you be so calm, Kurata?!

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:08.200
--the first-place person in that year's
competition played "Mizu no Hentai."
--Huh?! How can you be so calm, Kurata?!

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:09.620
--"Mizu no Hentai"?
--Doesn't her attitude tick you off?!

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:10.620
--"Hentai"...?
--Doesn't her attitude tick you off?!

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:13.830
--It's about water changing its form
to things like fog or clouds.
--She kept saying irritating things
with a serious look!

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:17.290
--You have to sing too and it's technically hard.
It's a very difficult piece.
--Argh! She makes my skin crawl!

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:20.370
You sing, too, while playing the koto?

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:24.500
In that competition, if no one is worthy
of first place, then no one receives the award.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.830
In other words...

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.750
Her ability has been proven.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.830
In which case, she's perfect
for improving our skills.

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:33.620
Mr. Takinami said it'd be fine, too.

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:37.330
But what if this decision is wrong...?

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:41.580
Hozy! You don't have to force yourself!

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:43.620
If you don't like it, it's okay to say so!

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:47.120
You don't have to think that this is for
the best for the club or anything!

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:49.790
Ahh... Once again...

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:54.120
I'm always being saved by them...

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:55.910
There's no longer time to hesitate

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:58.540
or shrink away from Miss Dojima
and her grandmother.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:02.750
So to them, it's their last chance.

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:04.950
Let's use her to the fullest.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.580
What?

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.870
Miss Dojima's ability has been proven.

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:13.910
Mr. Takinami said it'd be fine,
so I'm sure she'll teach us properly.

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:18.910
Let's learn as much as we can from her
as long as she teaches us properly.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:22.160
But if she doesn't...

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:24.450
...we'll just have to show her the door.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:26.910
Whoa... It's the dark Satowa!

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:29.540
Are you really sure, Hozuki?

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:34.410
Yes. I also think improving our
technique is necessary, so...

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:35.290
Okay.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:37.370
Kurata! What're you--

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:40.330
Continuing this discussion will get us nowhere.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:42.330
Let's try a lesson with her first.

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:44.950
Otherwise we can't make a decision.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:49.120
But would Chika accept that?

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:52.160
He's still practicing, so I'll go get him.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:11:01.790
It's quite a burden to teach others
while you're playing.

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:04.830
Her teaching must have been quite sloppy.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:08.910
I'm disappointed that their skill level
is lower than what I expected.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.330
Chika! Why don't you take a break?

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:14.200
We've been talking about Miss Dojima, and--

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:17.700
Hey, don't tell me you're asleep while play--

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.410
Chika...

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:34.500
Akira. How was the koto club?

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.410
Most of them haven't even mastered the basics.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:41.410
There's nothing to be concerned about.

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:44.700
Still, the only way to be certain
is to nip it in the bud now

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.410
no matter how small it is.

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:50.160
Make sure they clearly understand
the difference between their abilities

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:53.790
and that of a serious koto player.

00:11:53.790 --> 00:12:01.330
And make <i>her </i>aware that there's no longer
a place for her to play the koto.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:02.950
Understood.

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:18.250
How stupid...

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:32.120
Today, you'll first practice how to play
a single note firmly and carefully.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.000
A single note?!

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.120
We're starting with something
as basic as that <i>now</i>?

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:38.950
You practice it because you can't do it.
Now, please play.

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:46.750
Are you taking this lightly
because it's just a single note?

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:51.870
Every performance is comprised
of a connection of single notes.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:58.200
Play like this. Now, try it again.

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:01.250
Hozuki...

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:04.160
You don't have to do it, Satowa.

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:07.790
Well, it's important to go back
to the basics, so...

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:14.040
Next, play from the <i>kin </i>string
through the tenth continuously.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:18.620
Please play them so that you give
every single note the same weight.

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:21.620
Make sure that the notes sound even.

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:25.040
Play them at a fast tempo and go
down the scale one note at a time.

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:32.540
Hm? This should be a simple pattern,
but the notes sound kinda muddled.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.500
I can only hear muddled sounds.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:38.290
That's enough. Let's move on.

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:40.450
This is a variation of two-finger picking.

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:43.540
Go up the scale from strings 1 and 5,
2 and 7, 3 and 8, and so on.

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:47.120
Once you get to <i>kin</i>, go down
the scale in the same way.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:49.870
After that, play closer strings this time,

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:53.500
from 1 and 3, 2 and 4, 3 and 5, and so on,
and do the same thing but faster.

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.910
Please alternate and repeat this.

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:03.370
Is it possible that you all don't even realize
that your sounds are muddled?

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:07.660
You're not paying attention
to what each note sounds like at all.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:12.040
You take each note lightly and feel like
you can play because it sounds okay.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:14.660
If the volume of the sound
the paired fingers play isn't the same,

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:17.160
the notes won't be uniform.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:19.290
"The volume of the sound
the paired fingers play"...?

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.700
You play each note at a different volume.

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:25.370
That's why they're not uniform
and sound muddled.

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:28.290
And because of that,
the rhythm becomes disturbed.

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:37.410
This is what it means
for the notes to be uniform.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:42.290
Well then, everyone, try one more time.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:44.450
H-Hey, Chika!

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:48.200
What is it? If you have a problem
with me, you can just quit--

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.410
Play one more time.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.370
What?

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:56.500
I couldn't see it well because I was
sitting far away. So play one more time.

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.830
You should speak politely
when speaking to your teacher.

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.450
Please play it one more time.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:15.330
When using alternate picking,
don't use just your thumb.

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:20.620
These notes sound muddled, too, when these
patterns are in the pieces we play.

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:23.080
I thought I was playing them okay,

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:27.540
but when I play them separately,
they all sound unclear.

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:30.870
That's enough. This is getting nowhere.

00:15:30.870 --> 00:15:34.080
It's surprising that you're aiming
for nationals with your skill level.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:35.450
Hey, you don't have to say--

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:38.450
You're not worthy of playing "Tenkyu," yet.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:43.250
For today, please diligently practice
the basics we just went over.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:46.200
That is befitting for you.

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:55.700
Hozuki. It's okay to practice "Tenkyu"
at Ms. Nishina's place, right?

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:56.870
Yes, of course.

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:58.830
Also, today's...

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.870
Chika. What were you thinking?

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:06.040
Why did you readily follow
what that woman said?

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:07.540
What? "Why"?

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:10.870
That woman looks down
on Hozy as well as the club!

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:14.700
She's right! You're the one
who'd normally get upset first. But...!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.950
Because we're terrible players.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.120
What?

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:22.750
Because we're terrible players,
she looked down on Hozuki and the club.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.120
I wanna get better as soon as possible.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:29.950
And I'm definitely gonna go to nationals...

00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:32.700
...with everyone here.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:35.790
I'll use everything I can to do so.

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:40.580
I think it was Chika who was the most
frustrated when she looked down on us...

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:45.830
...because he loves this club
a lot more than we know, right?

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:53.790
Argh! I said something stupid!
I messed up again!

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:56.950
There are things we need to do
before we complain!

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:58.120
Right!

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:02.750
"The 36th National Koto Competition
Best Performance Award"

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:09.370
Let's first hammer out the basics
thoroughly as "befits" us!

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:15.080
Kudo! You're quite early!

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:17.450
Yeah.

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:20.120
You're probably keeping your hand too flat.

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:21.700
No, not like that.

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:23.040
I'm fine.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:23.870
What?

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:28.160
You don't have to worry about me.
Do your own practice.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:29.950
Are you stupid or what?

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:30.790
What?!

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:33.540
You're worried about what Mr. Takinami said.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:35.830
And you're honest to a fault, so you just
accepted it. I'm right, aren't I?

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:36.660
You really are stupid.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:38.250
You called me "stupid" three times!

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:40.750
I'm going to keep being
involved with your practice.

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:43.080
But if you do, your practice time will--

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:48.870
Let me be clear. Teaching everyone
has never been a burden to me.

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:50.830
Not even once.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:55.790
Now, move. The 17-string is hard
because the amount of strength you use

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:59.330
is different compared to the usual 13-string.

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:02.750
It's the same basics,

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:06.620
but depending on the player,
it really does sound totally different.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:09.750
Hozuki's tones are strong but somehow soft.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:12.410
And, how should I put it...

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:14.660
They are very clear.

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:18.200
Unlike my sounds, hers have
no unwanted noise at all.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:21.910
It sounds like every single note has meaning.

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:24.700
I wanna play like this, too!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:27.290
One more time!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:30.500
Hold it right there!

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:33.500
It's not fair that only Chika
is shown how to do it!

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.370
Hozuki! Please show us how to do it, too!

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:37.160
You're too close!

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:40.040
Jeez... What're you guys doing?

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:42.950
Good. Things are going back to normal.

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:46.450
Well, I was the one who was most irritated.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:52.250
But that's because you were
thinking about Hozuki the most.

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:57.160
That's why I thought it'd be okay
to accept Miss Dojima.

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:01.120
Oh, hey, guys. Got a minute?

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:02.450
What is it, four-eyes?

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:05.160
Well, about practicing the basics...

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:13.330
Four, two, three, four...

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:15.330
"Koto Club"
Four, two, three, four...

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:15.830
Four, two, three, four...

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:18.870
One, two, three, four...

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:21.950
Two, two, three, four...

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:22.580
--Three, two, three, four...

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:23.910
--What're they doing?
--Three, two, three, four...

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:25.040
--They said they made their own
arrangement of the basic practice.
--Three, two, three, four...

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:26.700
--They said they made their own
arrangement of the basic practice.
--Four, two, three, four...

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:28.160
--It seems that they are using the patterns
from "Tenkyu" containing the basics
--Four, two, three, four...

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:29.580
--It seems that they are using the patterns
from "Tenkyu" containing the basics
--One, two, three, four...

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:31.250
--so that it will help as much
as possible when they play it.
--One, two, three, four...

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:32.160
--so that it will help as much
as possible when they play it.
--Two, two, three, four...

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:34.330
--They all pitched in their ideas, like playing
the parts in order like a relay.
--Two, two, three, four...

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:36.450
--They all pitched in their ideas, like playing
the parts in order like a relay.
--Three, two, three, four...

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:37.410
--There are many others, too.
--Three, two, three, four...

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:39.000
--There are many others, too.
--Four, two, three, four...

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:40.450
--Interesting, isn't it?
--Four, two, three, four...

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:44.040
One, two, three, four...

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:45.410
Miss Dojima...

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.620
They haven't mastered the basics yet.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:50.000
Don't move onto a more
advanced level on your own.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:53.000
You all readily neglect the basics like that.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:57.160
We might want to use today to correct
your attitude towards the koto fir--

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:07.410
Kudo! Since when could he
play it so clearly...?

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.250
Whoa! Amazing! How the heck did he...?!

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:16.660
As always, he surprises me.

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:20.500
We're not neglecting them.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:24.200
His sounds are completely
different from before!

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:27.370
They weren't so different
from mine not too long ago!

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.830
Well, we don't have much
time left before the qualifier.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:31.410
So could you start giving lessons

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:34.870
on "Tenkyu" while doing the basic practice?

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:37.790
Okay.

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:39.950
Well then, I'll work with each part separately.

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:43.950
Please practice on your own until your turn.

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:48.370
Satowa... You don't need any lessons, right?

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:51.700
Oh no, please give me advice
if you think of anything.

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:54.950
<i>I </i>give <i>you </i>advice? You must be joking.

00:20:54.950 --> 00:21:00.290
I'm not joking. I heard that you won
that competition with "Mizu no Hentai."

00:21:00.290 --> 00:21:02.830
I think that's incredible.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:07.290
Can I ask you something?

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:08.290
Sure.

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:12.040
Why did you decide to do this piece?

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:14.500
Mr. Takinami suggested it.

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:18.790
I also thought it was a good opportunity
to finally face this piece.

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.660
"Face" it...?

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:22.410
I... see.

00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:25.750
Um... May I ask you something, too?

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:27.200
What is it?

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:31.160
I heard that you're
teaching us without any pay.

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:34.410
Doing it twice a week requires
quite a bit of your time.

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:36.290
Why would you go so far?

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:39.450
All this time...

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:43.870
All this time... All this time...
All this time...

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:48.790
I haven't been able to see
the light since that day.

00:21:48.790 --> 00:21:50.790
I just wanted to know what it was

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:53.040
that you wanted so badly
that you threw everything away

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:57.250
and even messed things up
for those around you.

00:21:57.250 --> 00:21:58.120
What?

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:00.370
It's this club, right?

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:03.000
I want to know its value.

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:04.700
That's all.

00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:08.830
I can't even remember the light.

00:23:50.120 --> 00:23:51.910
Next time, "Confrontation."

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:54.500
"#19 Confrontation"
